VERIFY-AND-FIX TASK

Workspace: {{workspace}}
Pipeline step: {{pipeline_step}}
Previous results: {{previous_results}}

The upstream random-audit step wrote AUDIT_REPORT.json to the workspace root and its verdict is in Previous results above. Read that file, build a finding ledger, and work one finding at a time: verify against the real code, then red-green-TDD a fix for every true finding. Clean up artifacts. Do not commit (a later step owns git).

RESULT shape (write to the RESULT file at the workspace root):
{
  "signal": "pass|fix|skip",
  "verdict": "PASS|FAIL|SKIP",
  "summary": "one sentence: N findings verified, M fixed, K skipped",
  "findings_processed": [
    { "id": "F001", "severity": "...", "location": "path:line",
      "state": "Fixed|Skipped", "tdd": "Red->Green | N/A - reason", "note": "..." }
  ],
  "build": { "compiles": true, "tests": "PASS|FAIL|N/A" },
  "stats": { "verified": 0, "fixed": 0, "skipped": 0 }
}

verdict PASS = at least one finding fixed and build green. FAIL = a fix broke build/regressions. SKIP = every finding was a false positive.
